{%- doc -%}
A logo drawn inside one image slide, between the slide's picture (and its blur) and its text: the slide's heading, text and buttons
are always in front of it. Styles are in sections/slideshow.liquid.

@param {object} logo - the logo image (the slide's "logo" setting)
@param {string} [position] - "top", "center" or "bottom": where the logo sits on the picture, touching that edge (no padding)
@param {boolean} [full] - true: the logo fills the slide inside the inner padding; false: it uses the widths below
@param {number} [mobile_width] - width in px on mobile when not full
@param {number} [desktop_width] - width in px on desktop when not full
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- if logo != blank -%}
  <div class="slideshow__logo slideshow__logo--{{ position | default: 'center' }}{% if full %} slideshow__logo--full{% endif %}" style="--slideshow-logo-width: {{ mobile_width | default: 300 }}px; --slideshow-logo-width-desktop: {{ desktop_width | default: 500 }}px;">
    {%- comment -%}
    When the slideshow's logo stands in for the header logo (the header logo is hidden while the header is transparent: "Hide the header logo",
    or "Logo scroll effect: Fly to the header"), it is a link to the same place as the header logo (the home page), so clicking it does what
    clicking the header logo did. Only the picture itself is clickable (the rest of the slide still swipes and clicks as before).
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.hide_header_logo or section.settings.logo_scroll_effect == 'fly' -%}
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="slideshow__logo-link" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
        {{- logo | image_url: width: 1600 | image_tag: sizes: '(max-width: 699px) 90vw, 60vw', widths: '200,300,400,600,800,1200,1600', alt: shop.name, loading: 'eager', decoding: 'sync', fetchpriority: 'low', draggable: 'false' -}}
      </a>
    {%- else -%}
      {{- logo | image_url: width: 1600 | image_tag: sizes: '(max-width: 699px) 90vw, 60vw', widths: '200,300,400,600,800,1200,1600', alt: shop.name, loading: 'eager', decoding: 'sync', fetchpriority: 'low' -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
